From: Vlad Zahorodnii
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 08:58:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fix announcing input method protocols

Backport of KWin merge request 9601 (commits 296e7c17 "Fix announcing
input method protocols" and 5bc7c913 "Announce privileged protocols to
input method", Vlad Zahorodnii, merged on master 2026-07-21) to 6.7.4,
whose filter has no sandbox branch: the check that keeps zwp_input_method_v1
and zwp_input_panel_v1 to KWin's own input method sat below the early
"not blacklisted, allowed" return and never ran, so any client could bind
them (a Fcitx 5 started by D-Bus activation in a Plasma Keyboard session
replaced KWin's input panel, row 71). The input method's own connection
gets every interface, as upstream's second commit has it.

Origin: backport, https://invent.kde.org/plasma/kwin/-/merge_requests/9601
Author: Vlad Zahorodnii
Applied-Upstream: master, 296e7c175e63923f4d064c04b636ae956915d37d and 5bc7c91394e64e80112b920fe7e082cbca377b60
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (the backport to 6.7.4's filter)
---
 src/wayland_server.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/wayland_server.cpp b/src/wayland_server.cpp
index 6e9b638..4523282 100644
--- a/src/wayland_server.cpp
+++ b/src/wayland_server.cpp
@@ -168,6 +168,12 @@ public:
             return false;
         }
 
+        if (client == waylandServer()->inputMethodConnection()) {
+            return true;
+        } else if (inputmethodInterfaces.contains(interfaceName)) {
+            return false;
+        }
+
         if (!interfacesBlackList.contains(interfaceName)) {
             return true;
         }
